window.docContents[150].resolve({"/Environment-and--___/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Environment-and--___--Memory-Safety":{"contents":"The cvc5 types for terms, sorts, solvers, etc. are all related to a notion of (term) manager\nresponsible for allocating and indexing terms and sorts. These types cannot interact and will\nproduce a runtime error if they do not agree on their manager.This API abstracts away the term manager completely and enforces manager consistency statically\nusing a type-class called Ω. Virtually all types in this library have an implicit Ω argument\nthat can be thought of as representing a specific term manager. On the sort Srt type for instance:#check Srt\nCvc.Srt [Ω] : Type\n\n\nΩ is an empty Prop type-class and will be erased at runtime; note that you cannot build an\ninstance yourself as the constructor is private.Argument of the Env monad representing a specific term manager.Ω is tied to cvc.lean's environment monad Env: Env α, or more precisely @Env Ω α,\ncorresponds to code that uses a specific term manager to produce a value of type α.\n\nThe first problem Ω and Env solve is that manipulating a value v tied to manager m after\nm has been freed is unsafe as freeing m frees v, so v should only live as long as m is\nalive. This is why most features in this library produce an Env _ output.Second, as mentioned above, values tied to different managers should never interact as that would\ncause a runtime error. By encoding a specific term manager through an Ω-value, we can type-check\nthat sorts/terms/solvers/etc. are compatible by making sure they agree on their Ω-value.To build an array-sort for instance, we must make sure the index and element sorts agree on their\nmanager, and keep track of the manager associated to the resulting sort.Create an array sort.* indexSort The array index sort.* elemSort The array element sort.\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level CVC5 API\u0009Environment and  Ω","header":"1.1. Memory Safety","id":"/Environment-and--___/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Environment-and--___--Memory-Safety"}});